Dear CIP friends,

as you know, B at D was released right before OSSJ started. I would like to 
thank the LF and the CIP board for doing the extra effort to go through 
the license clearance/approval process on time. I would also like to 
thank my colleagues at Codethink for putting extra hours on the release 
to make it happen right before the event.

++ B at D at the CIP open workshop

I invested about 20 min talking about what B at D is about and about the 
next steps in the CIP testing project. The intention is to repeat the 
workshop at ELCE. Hopefully there we will have a technical session and 
even a training session, if there is enough interest.

++ B at D at the CIP booth

I was happily surprised when I saw that Renesas made it and could show 
B at D working at the CIP booth on their new dev board to test the CIP 
kernel. They will need some time to publish and upstream the board 
support but they are working on it. It was a simple still great demo. 
Congrats.

